  {
   "xml_index": 4,
   "xml_name": "L08_004_Words As A Tuple",
   "display_name": "Words As A Tuple",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Conversions can be chained. <code>text.split()</code> gives a <b>list</b> of words, and <code>tuple(...)</code> turns that list into a tuple:</p>\n<pre>text = &quot;to be or not&quot;\nwords = text.split()\nprint(words)\nprint(tuple(words))</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>[&#x27;to&#x27;, &#x27;be&#x27;, &#x27;or&#x27;, &#x27;not&#x27;]\n(&#x27;to&#x27;, &#x27;be&#x27;, &#x27;or&#x27;, &#x27;not&#x27;)</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>word_tuple(text)</code>, which returns a tuple of the words in the string <code>text</code> (words are separated by spaces).</p>\n<p>For example, <code>word_tuple(\"to be or not\")</code> returns <code>('to', 'be', 'or', 'not')</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "def word_tuple(text):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(word_tuple(\"to be or not\"))\n",
