  {
   "xml_index": 7,
   "xml_name": "L08_007_Index And Slice A Tuple",
   "display_name": "Index And Slice A Tuple",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Indexing and slicing work on tuples exactly as on lists. A slice of a tuple is a new <b>tuple</b>:</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">-5</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">-4</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">-3</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">-2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">-1</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">t =</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">10</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(42,112,170);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">20</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(52,129,188);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">30</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(63,146,206);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">40</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">50</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">0</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">3</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">4</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#2e7a48;white-space:nowrap\">&uarr;<br>start</td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#7b3fa0;white-space:nowrap\">&uarr;<br>stop</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">t[1:4] is (20, 30, 40)</div>\n<pre>t = (10, 20, 30, 40, 50)\nprint(t[0], t[-1])\nprint(t[1:4])\nprint(t[::-1])</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>10 50\n(20, 30, 40)\n(50, 40, 30, 20, 10)</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write two functions for a tuple <code>t</code> with at least 2 items:</p>\n<ul><li><code>ends(t)</code> returns a tuple of its first and last items;</li><li><code>inside(t)</code> returns a tuple of all items except the first and the last.</li></ul>\n<p>For example, <code>ends((10, 20, 30, 40, 50))</code> returns <code>(10, 50)</code> and <code>inside((10, 20, 30, 40, 50))</code> returns <code>(20, 30, 40)</code>.</p>",
