  {
   "xml_index": 11,
   "xml_name": "L08_011_Tuples Cannot Change",
   "display_name": "Tuples Cannot Change",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Now the key idea. A tuple is <b>immutable</b>: once made, its items can never be replaced, added or removed. Trying gives a <code>TypeError</code>:</p>\n<pre>t = (1, 2, 3)\nt[0] = 100</pre>\n<pre style=\"color:#b3322a\">TypeError: &#x27;tuple&#x27; object does not support item assignment</pre>\n<p>There is also no <code>append</code>, <code>insert</code>, <code>remove</code> or <code>sort</code> for tuples. To get a \"changed\" tuple you build a <b>new</b> one, for example from slices and <code>+</code> (which joins tuples):</p>\n<pre>t = (1, 2, 3)\nnew = (100,) + t[1:]\nprint(new)\nprint(t)</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>(100, 2, 3)\n(1, 2, 3)</pre>\n<p>Note <code>(100,)</code>: to join a single value, first make it a one-item tuple.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>replace_item(t, i, x)</code>, which returns a new tuple equal to <code>t</code> but with the item at index <code>i</code> replaced by <code>x</code>. The index <code>i</code> is from 0 to <code>len(t) - 1</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>replace_item((1, 2, 3), 0, 100)</code> returns <code>(100, 2, 3)</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "def replace_item(t, i, x):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(replace_item((1, 2, 3), 0, 100))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(replace_item((1, 2, 3), 0, 100))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "(100, 2, 3)",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(replace_item((1, 2, 3), 2, 0))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "(1, 2, 0)",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "t = (\"a\",)\nprint(replace_item(t, 0, \"b\"), t)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "('b',) ('a',)",
     "extra": "",
