  {
   "xml_index": 12,
   "xml_name": "L08_012_Change Through A List",
   "display_name": "Change Through A List",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Another way to \"change\" a tuple uses the fact that <b>lists can change</b>:</p>\n<ol><li>convert the tuple to a list with <code>list(t)</code>;</li><li>change the list (<code>append</code>, <code>remove</code>, <code>sort</code>, <code>L[i] = ...</code>);</li><li>convert back with <code>tuple(L)</code>.</li></ol>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">-3</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">-2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">-1</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">t =</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(31,95,153);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;b&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(52,129,188);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;c&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(74,163,223);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;a&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">0</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">2</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">list(t), then change the list ...</div>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">L.sort() :</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(31,95,153);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;a&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(52,129,188);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;b&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(74,163,223);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;c&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">0</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">2</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">... then tuple(L) is (&#x27;a&#x27;, &#x27;b&#x27;, &#x27;c&#x27;), a new tuple. t itself never changed.</div>\n<pre>t = (&quot;b&quot;, &quot;c&quot;, &quot;a&quot;)\nL = list(t)\nL.sort()\nL.append(&quot;d&quot;)\nprint(tuple(L))\nprint(t)</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>(&#x27;a&#x27;, &#x27;b&#x27;, &#x27;c&#x27;, &#x27;d&#x27;)\n(&#x27;b&#x27;, &#x27;c&#x27;, &#x27;a&#x27;)</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>remove_value(t, x)</code>, which returns a new tuple: <code>t</code> without the first item equal to <code>x</code>. If <code>x</code> is not in <code>t</code>, return a tuple equal to <code>t</code>. (Tuples have no <code>remove</code> method, but lists do.)</p>\n<p>For example, <code>remove_value((3, 1, 4, 1), 1)</code> returns <code>(3, 4, 1)</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define remove_value(t, x): tuple -> list -> remove -> tuple.\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(remove_value((3, 1, 4, 1), 1))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(remove_value((3, 1, 4, 1), 1))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "(3, 4, 1)",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(remove_value((3, 1), 9))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "(3, 1)",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(remove_value((5,), 5))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "()",
     "extra": "",
