  {
   "xml_index": 14,
   "xml_name": "L08_014_Which Types Can Change",
   "display_name": "Which Types Can Change",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Here are the three sequence types side by side:</p>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;margin:6px 0 12px;font-size:14px\"><tr><th></th><th>string</th><th>list</th><th>tuple</th></tr><tr><td>written as</td><td><code>\"abc\"</code></td><td><code>[1, 2, 3]</code></td><td><code>(1, 2, 3)</code></td></tr><tr><td>items</td><td>characters</td><td>any values</td><td>any values</td></tr><tr><td>indexing, slicing, <code>len</code>, <code>in</code>, <code>for</code></td><td>yes</td><td>yes</td><td>yes</td></tr><tr><td>can be changed (mutable)?</td><td style=\"color:#b3322a\">no</td><td style=\"color:#2e7a48\">yes</td><td style=\"color:#b3322a\">no</td></tr><tr><td><code>x[0] = ...</code></td><td>TypeError</td><td>works</td><td>TypeError</td></tr><tr><td>methods that change it</td><td>none</td><td>append, insert, remove, pop, sort, ...</td><td>none</td></tr><tr><td>convert to it</td><td><code>\"\".join(...)</code></td><td><code>list(...)</code></td><td><code>tuple(...)</code></td></tr></table>\n<p><b>Python fact:</b> <code>type(x) == list</code> is <code>True</code> when <code>x</code> is a list; likewise <code>type(x) == tuple</code> and <code>type(x) == str</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>is_mutable(x)</code>, which returns <code>True</code> if <code>x</code> is a list, and <code>False</code> if it is a string or a tuple (only these three types are tested).</p>\n<p>For example, <code>is_mutable([1, 2])</code> returns <code>True</code> and <code>is_mutable((1, 2))</code> returns <code>False</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "def is_mutable(x):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(is_mutable([1, 2]))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(is_mutable([1, 2]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "True",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
