  {
   "xml_index": 16,
   "xml_name": "L08_016_Plus Equals Makes A New Tuple",
   "display_name": "Plus Equals Makes A New Tuple",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>If tuples cannot change, how can <code>t += (4,)</code> work? It does <b>not</b> change the tuple: it builds a <b>new</b> tuple <code>t + (4,)</code> and makes the name <code>t</code> point to it. Any other name for the old tuple still sees the old one. With a list, <code>+=</code> changes the list itself.</p>\n<p><b>Python fact:</b> <code>a is b</code> is <code>True</code> when <code>a</code> and <code>b</code> are the <b>same object</b> (not just equal).</p>\n<pre>t = (1, 2, 3)\nold = t\nt += (4,)\nprint(t, old, t is old)\n\nL = [1, 2, 3]\nold = L\nL += [4]\nprint(L, old, L is old)</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>(1, 2, 3, 4) (1, 2, 3) False\n[1, 2, 3, 4] [1, 2, 3, 4] True</pre>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop, function or class must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>grow(t, n)</code>, which returns a new tuple: the items of <code>t</code> followed by the numbers <code>1, 2, ..., n</code> (for a non-negative integer <code>n</code>). Build it in a loop with <code>+=</code>. The tuple <code>t</code> given to the function must not change (and cannot!).</p>\n<p>For example, <code>grow((9,), 3)</code> returns <code>(9, 1, 2, 3)</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define grow(t, n): add 1..n to the end, one at a time, with +=.\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(grow((9,), 3))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(grow((9,), 3))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "(9, 1, 2, 3)",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(grow((), 0))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "()",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "t = (5, 6)\nprint(grow(t, 2), t)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "(5, 6, 1, 2) (5, 6)",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(grow((), 5))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "(1, 2, 3, 4, 5)",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "t = ('a',)\ng = grow(t, 1)\nprint(g, t, g is t)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "('a', 1) ('a',) False",
     "extra": "",
