  {
   "xml_index": 19,
   "xml_name": "L08_019_Join And Repeat Tuples",
   "display_name": "Join And Repeat Tuples",
   "questiontext_html": "<p><code>+</code> joins two tuples into a new tuple, and <code>*</code> repeats a tuple (just like lists):</p>\n<pre>print((1, 2) + (3,))\nprint((&quot;ha&quot;,) * 3)\nprint((0,) * 4 + (1,))</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>(1, 2, 3)\n(&#x27;ha&#x27;, &#x27;ha&#x27;, &#x27;ha&#x27;)\n(0, 0, 0, 0, 1)</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>frame(t, x, n)</code>, which returns a new tuple: <code>n</code> copies of <code>x</code>, then the items of <code>t</code>, then <code>n</code> copies of <code>x</code> again (<code>n</code> is a non-negative integer).</p>\n<p>For example, <code>frame((5, 6), 0, 2)</code> returns <code>(0, 0, 5, 6, 0, 0)</code>.</p>",
