  {
   "xml_index": 21,
   "xml_name": "L08_021_Min Max Sum Of A Tuple",
   "display_name": "Min Max Sum Of A Tuple",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>The built-ins <code>min</code>, <code>max</code>, <code>sum</code> and <code>len</code> work on tuples of numbers just as on lists:</p>\n<pre>temps = (31, 28, 35)\nprint(min(temps), max(temps), sum(temps), len(temps))</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>28 35 94 3</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>summary(t)</code>, which returns a tuple <code>(smallest, largest, total, average)</code> for a non-empty tuple of integers <code>t</code>, with the average rounded to 2 decimal places with <code>round(value, 2)</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>summary((31, 28, 35))</code> returns <code>(28, 35, 94, 31.33)</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define summary(t): return (min, max, sum, average rounded to 2 places).\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(summary((31, 28, 35)))\n",
