  {
   "xml_index": 22,
   "xml_name": "L08_022_Comparing Tuples",
   "display_name": "Comparing Tuples",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Tuples can be compared with <code>&lt;</code>, <code>&gt;</code>, <code>==</code>. Python compares them <b>item by item from the left</b>, like words in a dictionary: the first items decide, and only if they are equal do the second items decide, and so on.</p>\n<p>This makes dates as <code>(year, month, day)</code> easy to compare:</p>\n<pre>print((2026, 3, 15) &lt; (2026, 10, 1))    # same year; month 3 &lt; 10\nprint((2025, 12, 31) &lt; (2026, 1, 1))    # the year decides\nprint((1, 2) == (1, 2), (1, 2) &lt; (1, 2, 0))</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>True\nTrue\nTrue True</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>earlier(d1, d2)</code>, where <code>d1</code> and <code>d2</code> are dates <code>(year, month, day)</code>. Return the date that comes first (if they are equal, return either).</p>\n<p>For example, <code>earlier((2026, 10, 1), (2026, 3, 15))</code> returns <code>(2026, 3, 15)</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define earlier(d1, d2).\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(earlier((2026, 10, 1), (2026, 3, 15)))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(earlier((2026, 10, 1), (2026, 3, 15)))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "(2026, 3, 15)",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(earlier((2025, 12, 31), (2026, 1, 1)))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "(2025, 12, 31)",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(earlier((2026, 5, 5), (2026, 5, 5)))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "(2026, 5, 5)",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(earlier((2026, 5, 20), (2026, 5, 3)))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "(2026, 5, 3)",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(earlier((1999, 1, 2), (2000, 1, 1)))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "(1999, 1, 2)",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
  },
