  {
   "xml_index": 25,
   "xml_name": "L08_025_Distance Between Points",
   "display_name": "Distance Between Points",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Now combine what you know about tuples and lists. There is less help from here on: plan first, then test with small examples, including the corner cases mentioned.</p>\n<p>The distance between points <code>(x1, y1)</code> and <code>(x2, y2)</code> is <code>((x2 - x1)<b>2 + (y2 - y1)</b>2) ** 0.5</code> (Pythagoras).</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>path_length(points)</code>, where <code>points</code> is a list of points <code>(x, y)</code> visited in order. Return the total length of the path (the sum of the distances between consecutive points), rounded to 2 decimal places with <code>round(value, 2)</code>. A list with fewer than 2 points has length <code>0</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>path_length([(0, 0), (3, 4), (3, 0)])</code> returns <code>9.0</code> (5 + 4).</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define path_length(points).\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(path_length([(0, 0), (3, 4), (3, 0)]))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(path_length([(0, 0), (3, 4), (3, 0)]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "9.0",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(path_length([(5, 5)]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "0",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(path_length([]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "0",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(path_length([(0, 0), (1, 1), (2, 2)]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "2.83",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(path_length([(-1, 0), (2, 4)]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "5.0",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
