  {
   "xml_index": 26,
   "xml_name": "L08_026_Rank By Marks",
   "display_name": "Rank By Marks",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Now combine what you know about tuples and lists. There is less help from here on: plan first, then test with small examples, including the corner cases mentioned.</p>\n<p>Hint: <code>sorted</code> sorts tuples by their <b>first</b> item (then the second, and so on). So to sort students by marks from high to low, and by name for equal marks, sort tuples <code>(-marks, name)</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>ranking(records)</code>, where <code>records</code> is a list of <code>(name, marks)</code> tuples. Return a list of the names, from the highest marks to the lowest; students with equal marks are listed in alphabetical order of name.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>ranking([(\"Ravi\", 67), (\"Asha\", 82), (\"Meera\", 82)])</code> returns <code>['Asha', 'Meera', 'Ravi']</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define ranking(records).\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(ranking([(\"Ravi\", 67), (\"Asha\", 82), (\"Meera\", 82)]))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(ranking([(\"Ravi\", 67), (\"Asha\", 82), (\"Meera\", 82)]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "['Asha', 'Meera', 'Ravi']",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(ranking([]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(ranking([(\"b\", 5), (\"a\", 5), (\"c\", 9)]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "['c', 'a', 'b']",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(ranking([(\"x\", 0), (\"y\", -2), (\"z\", 1)]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "['z', 'x', 'y']",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
