   "xml_name": "L08_027_Most Frequent Item",
   "display_name": "Most Frequent Item",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Now combine what you know about tuples and lists. There is less help from here on: plan first, then test with small examples, including the corner cases mentioned.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>most_frequent(t)</code>, where <code>t</code> is a non-empty tuple. Return a tuple <code>(item, count)</code>: the item that appears most often and how many times. If several items appear equally often, choose the one that appears <b>first</b> in <code>t</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>most_frequent((\"a\", \"b\", \"b\", \"a\", \"c\", \"b\"))</code> returns <code>('b', 3)</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define most_frequent(t).\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(most_frequent((\"a\", \"b\", \"b\", \"a\", \"c\", \"b\")))\n",
